    <p style="font-size:16px;"><strong style="color:#fde68a;">The big idea:</strong> Reconstruction was a bold attempt to rebuild the nation on the promise of freedom and equal citizenship; freedpeople achieved remarkable gains, but violence, economic pressure and fading Northern commitment reversed many of them — leaving an unfinished revolution whose constitutional legacy shaped later struggles for civil rights.</p>
